 "source": "The real dsh 0.2.1-rc.5 (`dsh --profile acp`) driven through weft's own agent server and this spec, against a local fake OpenAI-compatible model (scratchpad dsh/live/live.py and fake_model.py, a `fake` provider patched into the private home's profiles/acp/cordis.patch.yml; every line teed to dsh/live/wire.out.jsonl). initialize line 1, session/new line 2, session/resume line 21, session/set_config_option line 37; turns: hello lines 3-5, permission 6-12, reject 13-19, tool 22-27 (the `tool` step marks where dsh called weft's HTTP MCP server, between lines 23 and 24), bad key line 30, failed midway 31-34. `no key` is agents/dsh.transcript.jsonl line 12 (run1, no credentials). Nothing is composed. The tool turn was recorded again for real on DeepSeek Harness 0.2.1-rc.5, the program's tools weft's plugin (dsh_weft.mjs, inserted by the patch acp_dsh.py writes and hands over with --patch) forwarding to a stand-in of the MCP route, against a local scripted Anthropic Messages model through DEEPSEEK_BASE_URL (scratchpad rig/mock_model.py, acp_drive.py, rec_dsh.jsonl lines 6-11); the tool step stands where the plugin's call reached the route, and the patch's plugin config is where the stand-in finds the route (mcpFrom.list). `no balance` is real, on dsh 0.2.1-rc.5 with a real DeepSeek key whose account had no balance left (deepseek-official/deepseek-v4-flash; scratchpad acp12/dsh/transcript.jsonl): every prompt failed so, before any model output.",
